      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Engine: packages/engine-server/src/enginev2.ts",
      "description": "**This is the brain.** `DendronEngineV2` implements `DEngine`.\n\nIt owns:\n- Note indexing (full + incremental)\n- Schema validation & inheritance\n- Backlink / reference resolution\n- Vault management\n- Git integration + file watchers\n- SQLite usage for some indexes\n\nAlmost every command and webview ultimately talks to an engine instance (usually via the singleton `getEngine()`).\n\n[Open the engine class](./packages/engine-server/src/enginev2.ts)\n\n>> grep -n \"export class DendronEngineV2\" packages/engine-server/src/enginev2.ts",
      "file": "packages/engine-server/src/enginev2.ts",
      "line": 129,
      "selection": {
        "start": { "line": 129, "character": 1 },
        "end": { "line": 145, "character": 1 }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The Universal Type System: common-all",
      "description": "If you change anything in `common-all`, you will touch **every other package**.\n\nThis is where you find:\n- All the `NoteProps`, `DVault`, `DWorkspace`, `Schema` types\n- Constants (DENDRON_*)\n- Error classes, lookup types, publishing types, etc.\n- The `FName` / hierarchical note naming logic\n\n**Rule**: Put shared pure types and small utilities here. Everything else imports from here.\n\n[Open common-all package.json to see its exports](./packages/common-all/package.json)\n\nSee the dedicated package tour: [common-all Package Tour][common-all Deep Dive]",
      "directory": "packages/common-all"
    },
    {
      "title": "Markdown Superpowers: The unified Package",
      "description": "Dendron does **not** use VS Code's built-in markdown preview for its own features.\n\nAll special syntax (`[[wikilinks]]`, `![[note refs]]`, `^block-anchors`, `#tags`, frontmatter, etc.) goes through a custom remark/rehype pipeline defined here.\n\nThis pipeline powers:\n- The in-editor preview webview\n- Publishing (nextjs-template)\n- Graph view\n- Export pods\n- Backlink calculation (indirectly)\n\nUnderstanding this package is mandatory for any syntax or rendering work.\n\n[Open unified package entry](./packages/unified/src/index.ts)",
      "file": "packages/unified/src/index.ts",
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Native Module Hell: sqlite3 + webpack hacks (plugin-core)",
      "description": "This area is historically the #1 source of \"it worked yesterday, today the extension won't even activate\" after Node/VS Code upgrades.\n\nKey files you must know:\n- `packages/plugin-core/sqlite3-binding.js`\n- `packages/plugin-core/webpack-require-hack.js`\n- `packages/plugin-core/webpack.common.js` (the copy of .node binary)\n- The `binary` section in plugin-core package.json\n\n[Open the sqlite3 binding hack](./packages/plugin-core/sqlite3-binding.js)\n\nSee also `docs/dev/04-BUILD-AND-DEBUG-WORKFLOW.md` section on native modules.",
      "file": "packages/plugin-core/sqlite3-binding.js",
      "line": 1,
